{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Wildflower margins increase pollinator diversity on arable farms: a three-year paired-field study",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "O. Darwin, P. Wallace",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We surveyed pollinators on 24 paired fields (sown wildflower margin vs conventional grass margin) over three summers. Margins increased Shannon diversity by 0.41 (95 % CI 0.28–0.54) and bumblebee abundance by a factor of 2.3. Effects strengthened with margin age.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "pollinators · agri-environment · biodiversity · GLMM",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Keywords"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Insect pollinators have declined across Europe ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "potts2010"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Agri-environment schemes fund flower-rich margins, but evidence for their effect on diversity is mixed.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Methods",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Survey design",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Each farm contributed one treatment and one control field ≥ 500 m apart. Pollinators were recorded along fixed 100 m transects (6 visits per year, 10:00–16:00, > 15 °C, wind < Beaufort 4).",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Diversity indices",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "With ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "p_i",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the proportion of individuals in species ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "i",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "S",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " species:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "H' = -\\sum_{i=1}^{S} p_i \\ln p_i,\\qquad D = 1 - \\sum_{i=1}^{S} p_i^2,\\qquad J' = \\frac{H'}{\\ln S}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:div",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Statistical model",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Abundance counts were modelled with a negative-binomial GLMM with farm as random intercept:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\log \\mu_{ijt} = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1\\,\\text{Margin}_{ij} + \\beta_2\\,\\text{Year}_t + \\beta_3\\,(\\text{Margin}\\times\\text{Year})_{ijt} + u_i,\\quad u_i\\sim\\mathcal N(0,\\sigma_u^2).",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:glmm",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Metric",
          "Control",
          "Margin",
          "Ratio / diff.",
          "p"
        ],
        [
          "Total abundance",
          "31.2",
          "68.9",
          "×2.21",
          "< 0.001"
        ],
        [
          "Bumblebees",
          "8.4",
          "19.3",
          "×2.30",
          "< 0.001"
        ],
        [
          "Hoverflies",
          "12.1",
          "22.7",
          "×1.88",
          "< 0.001"
        ],
        [
          "Species richness",
          "9.8",
          "15.4",
          "+5.6",
          "< 0.001"
        ],
        [
          "Shannon H'",
          "1.72",
          "2.13",
          "+0.41",
          "< 0.001"
        ],
        [
          "Pielou J'",
          "0.75",
          "0.78",
          "+0.03",
          "0.21"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Mean per transect walk, pooled over years.",
      "label": "tab:eco",
      "alignment": "lrrrr",
      "style": "booktabs",
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Margin × Year interaction was positive (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\beta_3 = 0.18 \\pm 0.05",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "p = 0.002",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "), indicating accumulating benefit as sown species established.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Evenness was unchanged, so the diversity gain comes from additional species rather than redistribution. Landscape context was not controlled",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Semi-natural habitat within 1 km ranged from 3 % to 21 %.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        },
        {
          "text": ", which may explain between-farm variance (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\hat\\sigma_u = 0.34",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ").",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\begin{thebibliography}{99}\n\\bibitem{potts2010} S. G. Potts \\emph{et al.}, \\emph{Trends Ecol. Evol.} \\textbf{25}, 345 (2010).\n\\end{thebibliography}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    }
  ],
